{"tool_name":"bookend","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bookend","home":"https://github.com/Gregor-Mendel-Institute/bookend","license":"MIT","summary":"Bookend is a comprehensive framework for end-guided assembly of short-read, long-read, and end-capture RNA-seq data.","addition_date":"2022-09-02T18:22:02.404538Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:44:15.256818Z","tool_type":["Workbench"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:bookend","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"michael.nodine@wur.nl","name":"Michael D. Nodine","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6204-8857","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"michael.schon@wur.nl","name":"Michael A. Schon","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"public"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Mapping assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0523"},{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"},{"term":"Transcriptome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3258"}]}],"name":"Bookend","owner":"Chan019","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/s13059-022-02700-3","metadata":{"abstract":"We developed Bookend, a package for transcript assembly that incorporates data from different RNA-seq techniques, with a focus on identifying and utilizing RNA 5\u2032 and 3\u2032 ends. We demonstrate that correct identification of transcript start and end sites is essential for precise full-length transcript assembly. Utilization of end-labeled reads present in full-length single-cell RNA-seq datasets dramatically improves the precision of transcript assembly in single cells. Finally, we show that hybrid assembly across short-read, long-read, and end-capture RNA-seq datasets from Arabidopsis thaliana, as well as meta-assembly of RNA-seq from single mouse embryonic stem cells, can produce reference-quality end-to-end transcript annotations.","authors":[{"name":"Hofmann F."},{"name":"Lutzmayer S."},{"name":"Nodine M.D."},{"name"